# prettier-plugin-astro corrupts Alpine's dot-modifier attributes when the element sits
# inside a JSX expression block: it rewrites `x-intersect.once="…"` to
# `x-intersectωP_once="…"` and then fails to parse its own output. Both files below use
# `x-intersect.once` inside `{ cond && (…) }` / `.map(…)`. The attribute is fine in
# plain markup, so this is a plugin bug — contorting the markup to satisfy a formatter
# would be the wrong trade. Re-test on plugin upgrades and remove these lines when fixed.
